// flow/tools/verilator_waivers.vlt
//
// Shared Verilator lint waivers for known false-positives in TOOL-GENERATED RTL.
// This file is IP-agnostic: it matches by filename pattern, and peakrdl-regblock
// always names its outputs "<ip>_regblock.sv" / "<ip>_regblock_pkg.sv" for every
// IP, so any IP's static gate picks these waivers up automatically -- no per-IP
// waiver file needed.
//
// Convention (see CLAUDE.md "Generic-first" + docs/architecture.md "Known risks
// & mitigations: waivers require recorded justification"): never hand-edit files
// under */generated/* (they are clobbered on regeneration). If a real
// tool-false-positive originates in generated output, waive it here instead,
// with the justification recorded next to the rule below.
//
// Usage: add this file to the lint-tool's source list alongside the RTL, e.g.:
//   <tool> --lint-only -Wall ... flow/tools/verilator_waivers.vlt <rtl files...>

`verilator_config

// --- MULTIDRIVEN on `field_combo` (peakrdl-regblock generated *_regblock.sv) ---
// peakrdl-regblock packs every register field's transient control signals
// (next / load_next / ...) into members of one shared `field_combo` packed
// struct/union, and emits one always_comb block per field that drives only
// that field's own (bit-disjoint) member. Verilator's MULTIDRIVEN check
// operates at whole-variable granularity, not per-struct-member, so it flags
// this bit-disjoint, semantically-correct fan-out as if multiple processes
// drove the same net. This is a structural property of every peakrdl-regblock
// output, not a bug in any one IP's registers -- false positive, waived globally.
lint_off -rule MULTIDRIVEN -file "*_regblock.sv"

// --- UNUSEDPARAM on peakrdl-regblock generated *_regblock_pkg.sv ---
// peakrdl-regblock always emits DATA_WIDTH / MIN_ADDR_WIDTH / SIZE localparams
// in the generated package for downstream/documentation consumers (e.g. RAL,
// address decoders); the regblock module itself doesn't always reference all
// three internally. Harmless, structural to the generator -- waived globally.
lint_off -rule UNUSEDPARAM -file "*_regblock_pkg.sv"
